SUMMARY:Paul Winter Consort | Evening Performance
LOCATION:Bombyx\, 130 Pine St\, Florence\, MA 01062
DESCRIPTION:Celebrating The Winter Solstice\nIn 1980\, Paul Winter and the 
 Consort were invited to be artists-in-residence at New York’s Cathedral 
 of St. John the Divine. Paul Winter explains: “The dean had a personal m
 ission to create a bridge between spirituality and ecology. He appreciated
  our music\, but I think it was the ecological dimension of our repertoire
  that convinced him we could be part of the Cathedral. The premise of the 
 invitation was entirely secular\; it was not to have us play liturgical mu
 sic. We could present any events we wanted\, as long as we produced them o
 urselves.”\nhttps://bombyx.live/events/paul-winter-consort-evening-perfo
 rmance-2/\nFrom Pushpin Western Mass: https://pushpin.city/westernma/
